--[[
  MECHFALL // FORGE 77 — CET-only test mod
  ============================================================
  Companion layer for Titanfall BT-7274 (Quest and Companion), Nexus 35041.
  This file is generated by tools/generate.py from the JSON data files.

  WHAT IT IS: an ImGui overlay for hangar, subsystem authoring, forge params,
  reactor lab, settings, optional compat bridges, AND an IN-GAME PILOT tab that
  spawns / moves vanilla Cyberpunk 2077 entity records by TweakDB id and locks V
  into a cockpit / chase / orbit transform. Live power / mass / heat / RCS / ECM
  telemetry drives speed, brownout, thermal derate and in-world lock consequences.
  WHAT IT IS NOT: a new custom mech mesh or rig. It references game records only;
  no meshes, rigs, animations, VO, vehicle seats, mount systems or base-mod files
  are shipped. The browser test_build.html still owns the procedural 3D pilot test,
  the visual modeling table and the combat harness. Every game call is pcall-wrapped.

  NO base-mod files are bundled, edited or redistributed. Optional hooks are
  pcall-wrapped, user-triggered and never required. No ripped franchise assets.
  No redscript / TweakXL / ArchiveXL files in the installable path: those are
  .example templates only, because a syntax error in r6/scripts breaks the game.

  PATCH 2.31: this build targets CP2077 patch 2.31 and needs CET 1.37.1 (or
  1.37.0) + a 2.31-compatible RED4ext. CET 1.38.x supports patch 2.5 and drops
  older game patches. GetVersion() returns the CET build tag, so the IN-GAME
  PILOT tab selects the patch manually and warns on a mismatch. Phantom Liberty
  is optional; PL-only records are skipped unless explicitly enabled.

  FULL MODELS / TRACES: models.json supplies 30 example-only full models and
  front / side / top traces to the browser MODEL LIBRARY tab. Those 30 examples
  are the ONLY allowed model sources; no imported or extracted geometry.

  0.1.7-test: reactor balance is more forgiving (outputScale 56 + module bulk
  discount). weapons.json defines 8 custom weapon / shield categories. damage.json
  makes every part destructible: cockpit > 70% OR torso > 90% aggregate damage
  causes FULL DESTRUCTION + pilot emergency eject (X / mechfall_ig_eject).

  0.1.8-test: 10 ImGui tabs. models.json ships real triangulated 3D meshes +
  independent front/side/top traces; MF_DATA.models.examples drives in-game part
  placement. Designed weapons fire in CET; shields absorb and regenerate. Reactor
  coefficients / thresholds are generated (no stale hardcoded values) and
  tools/parity_test.js verifies CET <-> browser telemetry.
]]

